Package: oneplus-erhai-av1fix
Version: 1.1-test-01
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: TheMojoMan <themojoman@gmx.net>
Depends: libc6, libdrm2, libdav1d7, libgnutls30, libva2, libva-drm2
Conflicts: libva-av1fix, ffmpeg-av1fix
Replaces: libva-av1fix, ffmpeg-av1fix
Description: private AV1 VA-API client stack for the erhai players
 The erhai VA-API driver handles AV1 in two client classes.  Browsers submit
 whole framed OBUs and the driver parses the encoder's refresh set out of
 them, so they need nothing extra.  libavcodec (mpv, VLC, ffplay) submits
 headerless tile payloads, so the refresh set can only reach the driver as
 data - and VA-API's VADecPictureParameterBufferAV1 has no field for it.
 .
 This package carries the two libraries that fill that gap and installs them
 under /opt/oneplus-erhai-av1fix:
 . - libva 2.23.0 with the refresh_frame_flags pass-through
 . - FFmpeg 8.0.1 with the VA-API AV1 refresh set and loop-restoration fixes
   (built with libdav1d, gnutls/https and the full native codec set)
 .
 Nothing is installed into the system library path: Ubuntu keeps owning
 /usr/lib, so Firefox, Brave, the ffmpeg tools and every other client use the
 distribution libva/libav*.  The players reach the private stack through a
 small shim installed at their own absolute path (/usr/bin/vlc, /usr/bin/mpv,
 /usr/bin/ffplay; the real binary moves to <path>.erhai-orig behind a dpkg
 diversion), which only prepends /opt/oneplus-erhai-av1fix/lib to
 LD_LIBRARY_PATH.  A dpkg file trigger installs the shim again after any
 player install, upgrade or removal, so a newer upstream VLC keeps the fix.
 .
 The package also ships the patched va/ headers; build oneplus-erhai-video
 with PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/opt/oneplus-erhai-av1fix/lib/pkgconfig so the driver
 sees the refresh-frame fields.  It replaces the old libva-av1fix and
 ffmpeg-av1fix drop-ins (which shadowed the distribution libraries globally).
 .
 1.1 (2026-11-24): first published release, on top of oneplus-erhai-video 1.15.
 The libva 2.23.0 + FFmpeg 8.0.1 pair is unchanged from the test builds: FFmpeg
 is a distribution-style build (VA-API, VDPAU, libdav1d, gnutls), so a player
 built against it links cleanly, and nothing is installed into /usr/lib.
 Measured frame for frame against dav1d through the wrappers: t-720p60 600/600
 (376/600 when the client carries no refresh set), aom-altref 60/60,
 aom-tiles 40/40, 4K 16/16.
 .
 1.1-test-01 (2026-11-24): the PATH wrappers in /usr/local/bin are gone.  One
 shim now sits at each player's absolute path, with the real binary moved to
 <path>.erhai-orig behind a dpkg diversion, so clients that call /usr/bin/mpv
 or /usr/bin/vlc directly get the private stack too.  A dpkg file trigger
 reinstalls the shim after any VLC/mpv/ffmpeg install, upgrade or removal, and
 the postinst reports a player that links a libavcodec.so the private stack
 does not carry.
